Leftover Cleaner Prototype
0.1.0 — first prototype

Windows-only Python window for Notepad++.
Reads installed apps from the registry.
Scans AppData, ProgramData, and Temp for leftover folders.
Matches folder names to installed apps and shows a basic confidence score.
Shows size, a select box, and Delete.
Delete sends the folder to the Recycle Bin.
Dry-run is on by default.
Writes a log.
Refuses Windows system paths.

0.2.0 — stop deleting things that are still installed

Compares leftover folders with each app’s install location.
Skips a folder when an installed app still owns it.
Looks inside subfolders for leftovers that have no application.
Sort by path A–Z and Z–A.
Sort by size, largest to smallest.
Dark mode.
The version number is shown in the window title.

0.3.0 — tree and right-click

Paths are shown as a tree you can open and close.
Each row has a checkbox that selects and deselects.
Right-click menu: Delete, Open file location, Copy path.
Shift+F10 and the menu key open the same menu.
Deleting a row no longer collapses the whole tree.
Sorting no longer collapses the tree.
You can delete the parent folder that is holding the leftover files, not only the files inside it.

0.4.0 — better matching and uninstallers

Matching uses the folder name, the publisher, and the install folder together.
Confidence is higher only when more than one of those agrees.
Installed-apps tab lists official uninstallers and can run them.
Also finds leftover uninstallers such as unins000.exe and uninstall.exe.
The console stays open on a crash and writes the error instead of closing immediately.
Dark theme is applied before the window is built, so it no longer opens as a white window.

0.5.0 — hardware and speed

Reads the PC’s BIOS, CPU, and GPU from the registry.
Protects OEM folders that belong to that hardware: NVIDIA, Intel, AMD, Realtek, Dell, HP, Lenovo, ASUS, MSI, Acer, Gigabyte.
Protects a folder when a parent program, or a “father” program file, is still installed.
Skips Microsoft core components and other manufacturer core files.
Saves folder sizes in a cache so the next scan is faster.
Recycle Bin deletion refuses hardware and OEM paths.

0.5.2 — last prototype

Anything with Nahimic or A-Volute in the name is protected.
A crash writes crash.txt next to the script, says what failed, and opens that file.
Fixes for the window not opening: missing color settings, a bad theme line, and a broken indent.
This is the last version of leftover_cleaner.py. Later work moved to the drive scanner.

Microsoft App Remover 1.0.0
This is a different program, ms_app_remover.py. It does not scan leftover folders.

Lists Microsoft Store apps with PowerShell.
Lets you choose which optional ones to remove.
Locks Edge, Defender, the Store, Windows itself, framework packages, and anything Windows marks non-removable.
Asks you to make a System Restore point and can create that point.
Can relaunch itself as Administrator.
Dry-run stays on until you turn it off.
Dark window.
Writes a log of every action.
Does not delete System32, services, or drivers.

Leftover's (drive scanner)
0.6.0 — new scanner

New file, leftover_drive_scan.py. The old prototype was not extended.
Can scan C: and any other fixed or USB drive.
Includes Program Files and Program Files (x86).
Still skips Windows, personal documents, pictures, music, video, and desktop files.
Skips a folder when a running process or a Windows service is using it.
Local Ollama can review folders the rules are not sure about.
The app checks the model’s answer again and throws it out if the folder is protected.
The chosen model is saved in ai_link.json.
Link AI checks whether Ollama is installed, starts it, and can download a model.
Default model is hermes3.
Recently deleted items are listed from this tool and from the Recycle Bin.

0.7.0 — the agent is visible

ms_app_remover.py removed for further testing
The agent window opens when the cleaner opens.
It greets you, shows free space on each drive, the last scan time, and how much space was restored.
The agent writes its answer after a search finishes, not one word at a time.
A folder with its own .exe or shortcut is treated as still installed and is not recommended.
Right-click menu is in this program too: select, open location, copy path, run a leftover uninstaller, delete.

0.7.5 — stop at a program file

When a real program .exe or shortcut is found, scanning that folder stops and moves on.
Uninstallers do not count as the program. uninstall.exe and unins000.exe do not stop the scan.
At the end, a dialog lists every folder where scanning stopped.
The same list is written in the agent window.
Windows, OEM, Nahimic, installed apps, and in-use folders are still refused even if the model suggests them.

